  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "kxYySUB8vHTxImza+/KzdHg0Pz4=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:01.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Connect's modals are global state, not React context, so an editor opens one by calling a plain function rather than rendering a component. There is no `<Modal>` to mount and no provider to wrap.\n\nFive entry points:\n\n- `usePHModal(): PHModal | undefined` \u2014 reads whichever modal is currently displayed\n- `showPHModal(modal: PHModal)` \u2014 displays one; it is literally `setPHModal(modal)`\n- `closePHModal()` \u2014 `setPHModal(undefined)`\n- `showCreateDocumentModal(documentType)` and `showDeleteNodeModal(nodeOrId)` \u2014 typed shortcuts for the two cases editors reach for most\n\n`PHModal` is a discriminated union on `type`, with the payload each modal needs carried alongside. Source (`packages/reactor-browser/src/types/modals.ts`) has **19** members: `createDocument` (with an optional `documentModelVersion`), `deleteItem`, `addDrive`, `upgradeDrive`, `deleteDrive`, `driveSettings`, `settings`, `clearStorage`, `debugSettings`, `disclaimer`, `cookiesPolicy`, `downloadDocumentWithErrors`, `inspector`, `missingPackage`, `documentVersionUnsupported`, `confirmDocumentUpgrade`, `driveAuthRequired`, `openFileDocuments` (`modals.ts:44`) and `login` (`modals.ts:45`).\n\n```tsx\n<button onClick={() => showCreateDocumentModal(\"powerhouse/budget-statement\")}>\n  Create Budget Statement\n</button>\n```\n\nBecause it is a union, `showPHModal` is type-safe on the payload \u2014 `showPHModal({ type: \"deleteItem\" })` will not compile \u2014 and the same call is how built-in UI works: `ToolbarUpgradeButton` fires `showPHModal({ type: \"confirmDocumentUpgrade\", documentId })`, and `{ type: \"inspector\" }` is the programmatic route to the Inspector Modal.\n\n**Documentation caveat:** `01-ReactHooks.md` prints a 13-member union -- six short. It omits `missingPackage`, `documentVersionUnsupported`, `confirmDocumentUpgrade`, `driveAuthRequired`, `openFileDocuments` and `login`, misses `documentModelVersion` on `createDocument`, and names one member `exportDocumentWithErrors` where source says `downloadDocumentWithErrors`. Take member names from source.\n\n_Source: packages/reactor-browser/src/types/modals.ts and src/hooks/modals.ts, cross-checked against apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/05-EditorsUI/01-ReactHooks.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._\n\n_Source-verified 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse source at v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:01.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:01.000Z"
    }
  },
